# PhishVault-2 Stage 1: Ingestion & Deconstruction Walkthrough

I have implemented the generic Ingestion Engine logic to support normalizing URLs, Emails, and Files into a unified schema.

## Changes Created

### 1. Ingestion Engine Package (`services/ingestion/engine`)
- **Factory Pattern**: [ArtifactFactory](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/factory.go#11-14) handles routing artifacts to the correct processor.
- **Canonicalizer**: 
    - Decodes Punycode (`xn--` to Unicode).
    - Strips tracking parameters (`utm_`, `fbclid`, etc.).
    - Unwinds redirects (up to 12 hops) to find the final landing page.
- **Email Processor**:
    - Parses `.eml` / raw bytes.
    - Extracts Authentication Headers (SPF/DKIM).
    - Decomposes Multipart emails into Body and Attachments.
- **Attachment Processor**:
    - Calculates SHA256/MD5 hashes.
    - Detects content types.
    - Extracts URLs from text/html content using regex.

### 2. Service Integration
- Refactored [services/ingestion/main.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go) to use the new `engine`.
- [submitHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#55-118) now uses [CanonicalizerProcessor](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/canonicalizer.go#13-16).
- [submitEmailHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#119-184) now uses [EmailProcessor](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/email_processor.go#17-18) and supports multipart parsing.

